{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N1"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 118, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 4 absent, a conv on the direct input-to-output edge adds a much-needed path and capacity to node 3, giving positive gains (exps 6-10) versus negative changes when edge 4 already carries a conv (exps 1-5)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 5 is none the output node is starved of inputs, so adding a conv on edge 3 helps far more (exp 6 huge gain, exp 1 near-neutral versus negative for other edge-5 ops)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 3 when edge 4 is also absent leaves node 3 with at most one input or none at all, causing large accuracy drops (exps 21, 22, 27, 29)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is none, deleting edge 3 can disconnect the output entirely or leave a single weak path, producing catastrophic losses (exps 21, 23, 29)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing none with skip adds a new path from node 2 to the output (exps 45, 50 large gains), whereas replacing a conv with skip removes capacity (exps 43, 46, 47, 49)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv on the final edge for an identity loses learnable capacity, consistently hurting all three datasets (exps 43, 47, 49)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual input-to-output connection where none existed improves gradient flow and connectivity (exps 81, 85) far more than replacing an existing op on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the direct edge 3 path, a conv on edge 4 is critical for reaching the output (exp 91 huge, exp 92 solid) compared with small gains when edge 3 already has a conv (exps 93, 94)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 absent, node 2 receives little or no signal, so upgrading edge 5 has small or negative effect (exps 11, 12) versus large gains when edge 1 feeds node 2 (exps 13-18)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 2 is none, node 1 feeds the output only through edge 4 (often absent), so strengthening edge 0 brings little or negative change (exps 31, 32) versus consistent gains when edge 2 is active (exps 33-37)."}], "tok": 17142, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", 